      "content": "It's understandable that simple grounding techniques feel hollow when the core feeling is this vast emptiness. That sense of waiting for the final gust is a very real and heavy weight to carry. If the world feels too big and ungraspable, maybe the focus needs to shrink even further—not to find a solid place, but to find a tiny, quiet moment of just *being* without expectation. You don't have to hold onto anything right now; just allow yourself to exist in the space between the movement.",
